From ff986c69510c01d2ef3936bcad074939230fdd7d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: build-b-1 <build-b-1@warslop-dev>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 08:34:11 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] plugins: carry the answering route's own window on the
 response head

The app cannot see which route will serve a call (model choice and pools live in the router), so it must advertise and enforce the smallest window any route in the pool serves. When the router commits to the route that serves the call, its own context_length and max_output_tokens are now on the response head next to x-omniroute-route (warslop can then clamp the readback and name the real window in an overflow 400 instead of the pool floor).

onRoute may return windows_by_model (each dispatch id's own context_length and max_output_tokens, from the plugin's facts; no figure is ever guessed). The answering attempt's figures are echoed as x-omniroute-context-length and x-omniroute-max-output-tokens, and ride the in-band x_omniroute frame (context_length / max_output_tokens) when the early keepalive has already committed the head. Unknown figures are absent. Routing metadata only; integers only; only dispatched targets; failed combos get nothing.
